<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">This
release contains certain &ldquo;forward looking statements&rdquo; and certain &ldquo;forward-looking information&rdquo; as &lrm;defined
under applicable Canadian securities laws. Forward-looking statements and information can &lrm;generally be identified by the use of
forward-looking terminology such as &ldquo;may&rdquo;, &ldquo;will&rdquo;, &ldquo;expect&rdquo;, &ldquo;intend&rdquo;, &lrm;&lrm;&rdquo;estimate&rdquo;,
&ldquo;anticipate&rdquo;, &ldquo;believe&rdquo;, &ldquo;continue&rdquo;, &ldquo;plans&rdquo; or similar terminology. Forward-looking
statements included in this news release include, but are not limited to statements about: the timing and completion of the Consolidation;
the expected Effective Date of the Consolidation; the treatment of any fractional Common Shares in connection with the Consolidation;
the timing of and receipt of regulatory approval for the Consolidation; the Company&rsquo;s ability to meet the listing requirements
of the CSE and NASDAQ; the new CUSIP and ISIN of the Common Shares following the Consolidation; the anticipated effects of the Consolidation
as detailed in the consolidation Q&amp;A; and shareholders receiving a letter of transmittal.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Forward-looking
statements &lrm;and information are based on forecasts of future results, estimates of amounts not yet determinable and &lrm;assumptions
that, while believed by management to be reasonable, are inherently subject to significant &lrm;business, economic and competitive uncertainties
and contingencies. Forward-looking statements and &lrm;information are subject to various known and unknown risks and uncertainties,
many of which are beyond &lrm;the ability of the Company to control or predict, that may cause the Company&rsquo;s actual results, &lrm;performance
or achievements to be materially different from those expressed or implied thereby, and are &lrm;developed based on assumptions about
such risks, uncertainties and other factors set out here in, &lrm;including but not limited to: the financial condition, the successful
integration of technology, the inherent risks involved in &lrm;the general securities markets; uncertainties relating to the availability
and costs of financing needed in &lrm;the future; the inherent uncertainty of cost estimates and the potential for unexpected costs and
&lrm;expenses, currency fluctuations; regulatory restrictions, liability, competition, loss of key employees and &lrm;other related risks
and uncertainties disclosed under the heading &ldquo;Risk Factors&rdquo; in the Company&rsquo;s most &lrm;recent filings filed with securities
regulators in Canada on the SEDAR+ website at www.sedarplus.ca. The &lrm;Company undertakes no obligation to update forward-looking information
except as required by &lrm;applicable law. Such forward-looking information represents managements&rsquo; best judgment based on &lrm;information
currently available. No forward-looking statement can be guaranteed and actual future results &lrm;may vary materially. Accordingly,
readers are advised not to place undue reliance on forward-looking &lrm;statements or information.</FONT></P>

